IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `lpula-practice`
IMPORT `lpula-costs`

-- Legal Profession Uniform Law Application Act 2022 (WA), with the Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA) and the Uniform
-- Admission and General Rules it applies -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as
-- parameters.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's question form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. The Act and the Law it applies admit, certify and supervise lawyers and limit what their law practices may
-- charge; the client is the person those limits protect, and the person who may recover what an unqualified entity or a
-- void costs agreement took (Uniform Law ss 10(2), 185). Two seats:
--   - the law student, graduate or lawyer: the baseline's seat (lpula-practice.l4, lpula-costs.l4; Daniel in the WA
--     lives), 42 questions, one for each baseline export;
--   - the client of a law practice, or a person thinking of instructing one, 11 questions.
-- The law practice's duties in Part 4.3 are asked by the lawyer as what "my firm" may agree and recover, as the baseline
-- does. The Legal Practice Board, the Supreme Court, the Legal Costs Committee and the Legal Services and Complaints
-- Committee are never seats; what they may or must do appears as what it means for the person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the Graffiti Vandalism Act encoding). Within a role, a question that arises only in a
-- situation takes that situation's fact straight after `my role` (a second situation straight after the first), and
-- answers `does not arise for you` when it does not hold, without reading anything else. The questions of one situation
-- share one input, with one name, type and @desc, so the form asks it once. Three:
--   - `I have been admitted as a lawyer` (BOOLEAN; the lawyer's role only). The prerequisites for admission, the
--     compliance certificate and admission itself (Admission Rules rr 5, 6, Sch 2; Uniform Law ss 16-19; Application Act
--     ss 113, 114, 276, 279) arise only before admission: TRUE gives `does not arise for you`. The practising certificate,
--     supervision, titles, renewal and every costs question arise only after it: FALSE gives `does not arise for you`.
--     Whether the Law applies on a date, who decides, whether I am an Australian lawyer, and whether I may engage in legal
--     practice (and its penalties) arise either way (a graduate asks them too, d030).
--   - `the costs agreement in the matter` (`Costs agreement so far`; both roles). The conditional costs agreement
--     questions (its form, uplift, validity, cooling-off) arise only for a conditional costs agreement; the contingency
--     fee questions, the firm's penalty and the conduct matter (s 183 reaches any costs agreement) arise for any costs
--     agreement. `there is no costs agreement` gives `does not arise for you` for all of them; a costs agreement that is
--     not conditional gives it for the conditional ones.
--   - `the costs have been assessed` (BOOLEAN; both roles). Review of a costs assessment and repayment of the excess
--     (Application Act ss 149, 151) arise only after an assessment: FALSE gives `does not arise for you`.
--
-- The rules are in lpula-practice.l4 and lpula-costs.l4. This module calls them and restates none. For the lawyer each
-- answer, where its situations hold, is the baseline export's own answer, wrapped. For the client the baseline's
-- answers are reworded, value for value, where they speak as the lawyer ("my firm may recover nothing"), and two rules
-- the baseline does not export are helpers here (Uniform Law s 181(4), (5)). No exported question takes a DEONTIC or
-- EVENT input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Legal Profession Uniform Law Application Act 2022 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am studying law, seeking admission, or practising as a lawyer in WA`
    `I am a client of a law practice, or am thinking of instructing one`

-- The costs agreement situation (Uniform Law ss 179, 181(1)).
DECLARE `Costs agreement so far` IS ONE OF
    `there is no costs agreement`
    `a costs agreement that is not a conditional costs agreement`
    `a conditional costs agreement`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Penalty units` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `penalty units` HAS `how many` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Years` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    years HAS `how many years` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Months` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    months HAS `how many months` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Date, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the date is` HAS `the day` IS A DATE

-- The lawyer's answers: the baseline's own answer types, with `does not arise for you`.
DECLARE `Decision maker, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Decision maker`

DECLARE `Compliance certificate answer, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Compliance certificate answer`

DECLARE `Admission answer, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS AN `Admission answer`

DECLARE `My standing, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `My standing`

DECLARE `Certificate answer, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Certificate answer`

DECLARE `Old certificate answer, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS AN `Old certificate answer`

DECLARE `Practice answer, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Practice answer`

DECLARE `Renewal answer, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Renewal answer`

DECLARE `Agreement answer, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS AN `Agreement answer`

-- The client's answers, where the baseline speaks as the lawyer.
DECLARE `What the law practice may recover from me` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `valid: the law practice may enforce it like any other contract (s 184)`
    `void: a contingency fee, so the law practice may recover nothing for the services and must repay what you paid (s 185(4))`
    `void: the uplift breaches s 182, so the law practice may recover no part of the uplift fee from you (s 185(3))`
    `void: this matter cannot have a conditional costs agreement, so the law practice may recover no more than it could without one (s 185(1), (2))`
    `void: it fails the form requirements, so the law practice may recover no more than it could without one (s 185(1), (2))`

DECLARE `Cooling-off period` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `at least this many clear business days` HAS `how many days` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Recovery by an unqualified person` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `no: they were not entitled to engage in legal practice, so they may recover nothing for it and must repay what you paid, which you may recover from them as a debt (s 10(2))`
    `s 10(2) does not stop them recovering: they were entitled to do it, or it was not legal practice`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- The situation checks and the rewordings list every value and have no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31: a CONSIDER with
-- OTHERWISE takes the OTHERWISE branch for an ASSUMEd value instead of failing, so a case could not show the value was
-- not read).
GIVEN `the costs agreement in the matter` IS A `Costs agreement so far`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is no costs agreement in` `the costs agreement in the matter` IF
    CONSIDER `the costs agreement in the matter`
    WHEN `there is no costs agreement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a costs agreement that is not a conditional costs agreement` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a conditional costs agreement` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the costs agreement in the matter` IS A `Costs agreement so far`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is no conditional costs agreement in` `the costs agreement in the matter` IF
    CONSIDER `the costs agreement in the matter`
    WHEN `there is no costs agreement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a costs agreement that is not a conditional costs agreement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a conditional costs agreement` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the answer` IS AN `Agreement answer`
GIVETH A `What the law practice may recover from me`
`for the client, the agreement answer` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `valid: it may be enforced like any other contract (s 184)` THEN `valid: the law practice may enforce it like any other contract (s 184)`
    WHEN `void: a contingency fee, so my firm may recover nothing for the services and must repay what it received (s 185(4))` THEN `void: a contingency fee, so the law practice may recover nothing for the services and must repay what you paid (s 185(4))`
    WHEN `void: the uplift breaches s 182, so no part of the uplift fee is recoverable (s 185(3))` THEN `void: the uplift breaches s 182, so the law practice may recover no part of the uplift fee from you (s 185(3))`
    WHEN `void: this matter cannot have a conditional costs agreement, so no more is recoverable than without it (s 185(1), (2))` THEN `void: this matter cannot have a conditional costs agreement, so the law practice may recover no more than it could without one (s 185(1), (2))`
    WHEN `void: it fails the form requirements, so no more is recoverable than without it (s 185(1), (2))` THEN `void: it fails the form requirements, so the law practice may recover no more than it could without one (s 185(1), (2))`

-- Uniform Law s 10(2): "An entity is not entitled to recover any amount, and must repay any amount received, in respect of
-- anything the entity did in contravention of subsection (1). Any amount so received may be recovered as a debt by the
-- person who paid it." Whether the person contravened s 10(1) is the baseline's `May I engage in legal practice`, asked
-- of the person who did the work.
GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Practice answer`
GIVETH A `Recovery by an unqualified person`
`for the client, what s 10(2) says of` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `yes: as an Australian legal practitioner I am entitled to (Uniform Law s 43), subject to my certificate's conditions` THEN `s 10(2) does not stop them recovering: they were entitled to do it, or it was not legal practice`
    WHEN `yes: I am a qualified entity under another law (Uniform Law s 6, para (d))` THEN `s 10(2) does not stop them recovering: they were entitled to do it, or it was not legal practice`
    WHEN `yes: I am exempt under General Rules r 10` THEN `s 10(2) does not stop them recovering: they were entitled to do it, or it was not legal practice`
    WHEN `yes: policy work is not engaging in legal practice (Uniform Law s 6)` THEN `s 10(2) does not stop them recovering: they were entitled to do it, or it was not legal practice`
    WHEN `no: it would be an offence under Uniform Law s 10(1), and I could keep no fee for it (s 10(2))` THEN `no: they were not entitled to engage in legal practice, so they may recover nothing for it and must repay what you paid, which you may recover from them as a debt (s 10(2))`

-- Uniform Law s 181(4): "A conditional costs agreement must contain a cooling-off period of not less than 5 clear
-- business days during which the client, by written notice, may terminate the agreement, but this requirement does not
-- apply where the agreement is made between law practices only." The client here is not a law practice. Not exported by
-- the baseline (it reads the period as a term of the agreement, in its form check).
`s 181(4) -- the least cooling-off period, in clear business days` MEANS 5

-- s 181(5): "If a client terminates a conditional costs agreement within the cooling-off period, the law practice -- (a)
-- may recover only those legal costs in respect of legal services performed for the client before that termination that
-- were performed on the instructions of the client and with the client's knowledge that the legal services would be
-- performed during that period; and (b) in particular, may not recover any uplift fee." Not in the baseline.
`s 181(5)(b) -- an uplift fee is recoverable after a termination in the cooling-off period` MEANS FALSE

§§ `For the law student, graduate or lawyer`

§§§ `Application Act ss 6, 7, 20 -- does the Uniform Law apply, and who decides`

@export Does the Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA) govern my admission and practice on this date (Application Act ss 6, 7)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the date` IS A DATE @desc The date you are asking about
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does the Uniform Law govern my admission and practice on this date` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am studying law, seeking admission, or practising as a lawyer in WA` THEN
        `yes if` (`Does the Uniform Law govern my admission and practice on` `the date`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Who decides this for me in WA (Application Act s 20)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what I want decided` IS A `What I want decided` @desc What you want decided
GIVETH A `Decision maker, if it arises`
`Who decides this for me in WA` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am studying law, seeking admission, or practising as a lawyer in WA` THEN
        `the answer is` (`Who decides this for me` `what I want decided`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Admission Rules rr 5, 6, Sch 2 cl 4; Application Act ss 278, 279 -- the prerequisites for admission`

@export Have I attained the academic qualifications prerequisite for admission (Uniform Law s 17(1)(a), Admission Rules r 5(1), Application Act s 278)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been admitted as a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been admitted to the Australian legal profession, in WA or in another Australian jurisdiction, under the Uniform Law or under the earlier law
      `the course` IS A `My law course` @desc Your law degree or other law course
      `old Act qualifications obtained before 1 July 2022` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you obtained approved or corresponding academic qualifications under the Legal Profession Act 2008 before 1 July 2022
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have I attained the academic qualifications prerequisite for admission` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am studying law, seeking admission, or practising as a lawyer in WA` THEN
        IF `I have been admitted as a lawyer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Have I attained the academic qualifications prerequisite` `the course` `old Act qualifications obtained before 1 July 2022`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does my practical legal training under the old Act carry over into the Uniform Law (Application Act s 279)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been admitted as a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been admitted to the Australian legal profession, in WA or in another Australian jurisdiction, under the Uniform Law or under the earlier law
      `I began it before 1 July 2022` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you began old-Act practical legal training before 1 July 2022
      `the date I completed it` IS A DATE @desc The date you completed it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my practical legal training under the old Act carry over` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am studying law, seeking admission, or practising as a lawyer in WA` THEN
        IF `I have been admitted as a lawyer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does section 279 carry my old PLT over` `I began it before 1 July 2022` `the date I completed it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Have I completed the practical legal training prerequisite for admission (Uniform Law s 17(1)(b), Admission Rules r 6(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been admitted as a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been admitted to the Australian legal profession, in WA or in another Australian jurisdiction, under the Uniform Law or under the earlier law
      `the training` IS A `My practical legal training` @desc Your practical legal training
      `carried over by section 279` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Application Act s 279 carries your old-Act practical legal training over
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have I completed the practical legal training prerequisite for admission` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am studying law, seeking admission, or practising as a lawyer in WA` THEN
        IF `I have been admitted as a lawyer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Have I completed the practical legal training prerequisite` `the training` `carried over by section 279`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I start my practical legal training now (Admission Rules r 6(3), Schedule 2 cl 4)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been admitted as a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been admitted to the Australian legal profession, in WA or in another Australian jurisdiction, under the Uniform Law or under the earlier law
      `the form` IS A `PLT form` @desc The form of PLT you want to start
      `I have completed an accredited law course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have completed your accredited law course
      `academic subjects left` IS A NUMBER @desc How many academic subjects you still have to complete
      `one of them is a Schedule 1 area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any subject left is one of the Schedule 1 academic areas
      `enrolled in them during the PLT` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you will be enrolled in them while doing the PLT course
      `the Board gave prior permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has given you prior permission
      `an integrated program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the PLT is part of an integrated program of academic study and PLT
      `the Board otherwise determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has otherwise determined you may start
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I start my practical legal training now` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am studying law, seeking admission, or practising as a lawyer in WA` THEN
        IF `I have been admitted as a lawyer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I start my PLT now` `the form` `I have completed an accredited law course` `academic subjects left` `one of them is a Schedule 1 area` `enrolled in them during the PLT` `the Board gave prior permission` `an integrated program` `the Board otherwise determined`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the Board require more study or training of me because I qualified more than 5 years before applying (Admission Rules rr 5(2), 6(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been admitted as a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been admitted to the Australian legal profession, in WA or in another Australian jurisdiction, under the Uniform Law or under the earlier law
      `the date I completed the course or the training` IS A DATE @desc The date you completed the law course (or the practical legal training)
      `the date I apply for a compliance certificate` IS A DATE @desc The date you apply for a compliance certificate
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Board require more of me because my qualification is more than 5 years old` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am studying law, seeking admission, or practising as a lawyer in WA` THEN
        IF `I have been admitted as a lawyer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can the Board require more because my qualification is old` `the date I completed the course or the training` `the date I apply for a compliance certificate`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Uniform Law ss 16-19; Application Act ss 113, 114, 276 -- the compliance certificate and admission`

@export Can the Board issue me a compliance certificate for admission (Uniform Law ss 17-19, Admission Rules rr 5, 6, 10)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been admitted as a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been admitted to the Australian legal profession, in WA or in another Australian jurisdiction, under the Uniform Law or under the earlier law
      `the course` IS A `My law course` @desc Your law degree or other law course
      `old Act qualifications obtained before 1 July 2022` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you obtained approved or corresponding academic qualifications under the Legal Profession Act 2008 before 1 July 2022
      `the training` IS A `My practical legal training` @desc Your practical legal training
      `carried over by section 279` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Application Act s 279 carries your old-Act practical legal training over
      `exempted from the academic prerequisite` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has exempted you under Uniform Law s 18
      `exempted from the PLT prerequisite` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has exempted you under Uniform Law s 18
      `the Board is satisfied I am fit and proper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board is satisfied you are a fit and proper person
      `notice given and objections dealt with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has published notice and dealt with any objections (s 19(8))
GIVETH A `Compliance certificate answer, if it arises`
`Can the Board issue me a compliance certificate for admission` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am studying law, seeking admission, or practising as a lawyer in WA` THEN
        IF `I have been admitted as a lawyer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the answer is` (`Can the Board issue me a compliance certificate` `the course` `old Act qualifications obtained before 1 July 2022` `the training` `carried over by section 279` `exempted from the academic prerequisite` `exempted from the PLT prerequisite` `the Board is satisfied I am fit and proper` `notice given and objections dealt with`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the Supreme Court of WA admit me as an Australian lawyer (Uniform Law s 16, Application Act ss 113, 114)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been admitted as a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been admitted to the Australian legal profession, in WA or in another Australian jurisdiction, under the Uniform Law or under the earlier law
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the admission date` IS A DATE @desc The date of the admission sitting
      `a compliance certificate in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has provided the Court with a compliance certificate that is still in force
      `already admitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are already admitted to the Australian legal profession
      `I take the oath or affirmation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you take the oath or make the affirmation of office
      `my admission application` IS A `My admission application` @desc How you applied for admission
      `judges sitting` IS A NUMBER @desc How many judges constitute the Court
GIVETH AN `Admission answer, if it arises`
`May the Supreme Court of WA admit me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am studying law, seeking admission, or practising as a lawyer in WA` THEN
        IF `I have been admitted as a lawyer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the answer is` (`May the Supreme Court admit me` `my date of birth` `the admission date` `a compliance certificate in force` `already admitted` `I take the oath or affirmation` `my admission application` `judges sitting`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does my admission application under the old Act continue as an application under Application Act s 113 (Application Act s 276)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been admitted as a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been admitted to the Australian legal profession, in WA or in another Australian jurisdiction, under the Uniform Law or under the earlier law
      `the date I applied` IS A DATE @desc The date you applied under s 25(1) of the Legal Profession Act 2008
      `decided before 1 July 2022` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was decided before 1 July 2022
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my admission application under the old Act continue` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am studying law, seeking admission, or practising as a lawyer in WA` THEN
        IF `I have been admitted as a lawyer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does my old admission application continue` `the date I applied` `decided before 1 July 2022`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Uniform Law ss 6, 10, 22, 43, Sch 4 cl 11; General Rules r 10 -- am I a lawyer, and may I practise`

@export Am I an Australian lawyer on this date (Uniform Law ss 6, 22(2), Sch 4 cl 11, Application Act s 322)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the date` IS A DATE @desc The date you are asking about
      `I signed the Supreme Court roll under the Uniform Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were admitted under the Uniform Law and signed the roll
      `admitted in another Australian jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are admitted in another Australian jurisdiction
      `admitted in WA under the old Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were admitted by the Supreme Court of WA under the Legal Profession Act 2008 (or earlier)
      `removed from the roll` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your name has been removed from the roll
GIVETH A `My standing, if it arises`
`Am I an Australian lawyer on this date` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am studying law, seeking admission, or practising as a lawyer in WA` THEN
        `the answer is` (`Am I an Australian lawyer` `the date` `I signed the Supreme Court roll under the Uniform Law` `admitted in another Australian jurisdiction` `admitted in WA under the old Act` `removed from the roll`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is my day of admission, if I was admitted in WA under the old Act (Uniform Law Sch 4 cl 11(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been admitted as a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been admitted to the Australian legal profession, in WA or in another Australian jurisdiction, under the Uniform Law or under the earlier law
      `the day I was admitted under the old Act` IS A DATE @desc The day the Supreme Court admitted you under the old Act
GIVETH A `Date, if it arises`
`What is my day of admission, if I was admitted under the old Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am studying law, seeking admission, or practising as a lawyer in WA` THEN
        IF NOT (`I have been admitted as a lawyer`)
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the date is` (`What is my day of admission` `the day I was admitted under the old Act`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I engage in legal practice in WA (Uniform Law ss 6, 10, 43, General Rules r 10)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what I want to do` IS A `What I want to do` @desc What you want to do
      `my standing` IS A `My standing` @desc Whether you are an Australian lawyer
      `I hold a current practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a current Australian practising certificate
      `authorised by another law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a law of the Commonwealth or a State, other than the Uniform Law, authorises you to engage in legal practice
      `exempt under General Rules r 10` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a General Rules r 10 exemption covers what you do (for example a licensed conveyancer)
GIVETH A `Practice answer, if it arises`
`May I engage in legal practice in WA` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am studying law, seeking admission, or practising as a lawyer in WA` THEN
        `the answer is` (`May I engage in legal practice` `what I want to do` `my standing` `I hold a current practising certificate` `authorised by another law` `exempt under General Rules r 10`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined, in penalty units, for engaging in legal practice when not entitled (Uniform Law s 10(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Penalty units`
`What is the most I can be fined for engaging in legal practice when not entitled` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am studying law, seeking admission, or practising as a lawyer in WA` THEN
        `penalty units` `What is the most I can be fined for unqualified practice`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the longest I can be imprisoned, in years, for engaging in legal practice when not entitled (Uniform Law s 10(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Years`
`What is the longest I can be imprisoned for engaging in legal practice when not entitled` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am studying law, seeking admission, or practising as a lawyer in WA` THEN
