        IF NOT (`I have been admitted as a lawyer`)
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does a costs determination govern my fees` `the position`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Has my firm breached its duty to tell the client whether a costs determination applies (Application Act s 143)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been admitted as a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been admitted to the Australian legal profession, in WA or in another Australian jurisdiction, under the Uniform Law or under the earlier law
      `we gave the Uniform Law s 174(1)(a) disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your firm gave the client the s 174(1)(a) costs disclosure
      `we said whether a costs determination applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it also told the client whether a costs determination applies
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Has my firm breached its duty to say whether a costs determination applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am studying law, seeking admission, or practising as a lawyer in WA` THEN
        IF NOT (`I have been admitted as a lawyer`)
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Has my firm breached section 143` `we gave the Uniform Law s 174(1)(a) disclosure` `we said whether a costs determination applies`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Application Act ss 149, 151 -- after a costs assessment`

@export Can I still apply to the Supreme Court for review of the costs assessment (Application Act s 149(2)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been admitted as a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been admitted to the Australian legal profession, in WA or in another Australian jurisdiction, under the Uniform Law or under the earlier law
      `the costs have been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the legal costs in the matter have been assessed under the Uniform Law and you have been notified of the assessment
      `the date I was notified` IS A DATE @desc The date you were notified of the costs assessment
      `the date I apply for review` IS A DATE @desc The date of the application for review
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I still apply to the Supreme Court for review of the costs assessment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am studying law, seeking admission, or practising as a lawyer in WA` THEN
        IF NOT (`I have been admitted as a lawyer`)
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE IF NOT (`the costs have been assessed`)
             THEN `does not arise for you`
             ELSE `yes if` (`Can I still apply for review of the assessment` `the date I was notified` `the date I apply for review`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much must my firm repay as excess over the assessed costs (Application Act s 151)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been admitted as a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been admitted to the Australian legal profession, in WA or in another Australian jurisdiction, under the Uniform Law or under the earlier law
      `the costs have been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the legal costs in the matter have been assessed under the Uniform Law and you have been notified of the assessment
      `what the client paid` IS A NUMBER @desc What the client paid as legal costs, in dollars
      `the assessed costs` IS A NUMBER @desc The legal costs determined on assessment, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much must my firm repay as excess over the assessed costs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am studying law, seeking admission, or practising as a lawyer in WA` THEN
        IF NOT (`I have been admitted as a lawyer`)
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE IF NOT (`the costs have been assessed`)
             THEN `does not arise for you`
             ELSE amount (`How much must my firm repay` `what the client paid` `the assessed costs`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
§§ `For the client of a law practice`

§§§ `Uniform Law Part 4.3, Sch 4 cl 18, ss 181-185 -- my costs agreement`

@export Does Uniform Law Part 4.3 (legal costs) govern the costs of my matter: did I first instruct the law practice on or after 1 July 2022 (Uniform Law Sch 4 cl 18)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the date I first instructed the law practice` IS A DATE @desc The date you first instructed the law practice in the matter
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does Uniform Law Part 4.3 govern the legal costs of my matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a client of a law practice, or am thinking of instructing one` THEN `yes if` (`Does Part 4.3 govern my fees in this matter` `the date I first instructed the law practice`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the law practice's costs agreement with me for this matter be a conditional costs agreement, with fees payable only on a successful outcome (Uniform Law s 181(7))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the matter` IS A `My matter` @desc What kind of matter it is
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the law practice's costs agreement with me be a conditional costs agreement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a client of a law practice, or am thinking of instructing one` THEN `yes if` (`May the costs agreement be conditional for this matter` `the matter`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my conditional costs agreement with the law practice valid, and if not, what may the law practice recover from me (Uniform Law ss 181-185)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the costs agreement in the matter` IS A `Costs agreement so far` @desc Whether there is a costs agreement between the law practice and the client in the matter, and if so whether it is a conditional costs agreement (some or all of the legal costs payable only on a successful outcome, Uniform Law s 181(1))
      `the matter` IS A `My matter` @desc What kind of matter it is
      `reading an arbitral tribunal as a tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether to read "tribunal" in Uniform Law s 6 as including an arbitral tribunal (the text does not settle it)
      `court or tribunal proceedings are reasonably likely` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether proceedings in a court or tribunal are reasonably likely (for an arbitration: a stay or enforcement application)
      `the agreement` IS A `My conditional costs agreement` @desc The terms of the costs agreement
GIVETH A `What the law practice may recover from me`
`Is my conditional costs agreement with the law practice valid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a client of a law practice, or am thinking of instructing one` THEN
        IF `there is no conditional costs agreement in` `the costs agreement in the matter`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `for the client, the agreement answer` (`Is my conditional costs agreement valid` `the matter` `reading an arbitral tribunal as a tribunal` `court or tribunal proceedings are reasonably likely` `the agreement`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export For how many clear business days, at least, may I end my conditional costs agreement by written notice (the cooling-off period, Uniform Law s 181(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the costs agreement in the matter` IS A `Costs agreement so far` @desc Whether there is a costs agreement between the law practice and the client in the matter, and if so whether it is a conditional costs agreement (some or all of the legal costs payable only on a successful outcome, Uniform Law s 181(1))
GIVETH A `Cooling-off period`
`How long is my cooling-off period under a conditional costs agreement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a client of a law practice, or am thinking of instructing one` THEN
        IF `there is no conditional costs agreement in` `the costs agreement in the matter`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `at least this many clear business days` `s 181(4) -- the least cooling-off period, in clear business days`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If I end my conditional costs agreement within the cooling-off period, may the law practice still recover an uplift fee from me (Uniform Law s 181(5); it may recover only the costs of work done before then on my instructions and with my knowledge)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the costs agreement in the matter` IS A `Costs agreement so far` @desc Whether there is a costs agreement between the law practice and the client in the matter, and if so whether it is a conditional costs agreement (some or all of the legal costs payable only on a successful outcome, Uniform Law s 181(1))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`If I end the agreement in the cooling-off period may the law practice recover an uplift fee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a client of a law practice, or am thinking of instructing one` THEN
        IF `there is no conditional costs agreement in` `the costs agreement in the matter`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` `s 181(5)(b) -- an uplift fee is recoverable after a termination in the cooling-off period`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is the fee in my costs agreement a prohibited contingency fee, worked out on the amount of an award or settlement (Uniform Law s 183, Application Act s 136)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the costs agreement in the matter` IS A `Costs agreement so far` @desc Whether there is a costs agreement between the law practice and the client in the matter, and if so whether it is a conditional costs agreement (some or all of the legal costs payable only on a successful outcome, Uniform Law s 181(1))
      `the agreement` IS A `My conditional costs agreement` @desc The terms of the costs agreement
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the fee in my costs agreement a prohibited contingency fee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a client of a law practice, or am thinking of instructing one` THEN
        IF `there is no costs agreement in` `the costs agreement in the matter`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is the agreement a prohibited contingency fee` `the agreement`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Application Act ss 141, 143 -- WA costs determinations`

@export Does a WA costs determination govern what the law practice may charge me (Application Act s 141)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the position` IS A `My costs position` @desc The determination, agreement and orders in the matter
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does a WA costs determination govern what the law practice may charge me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a client of a law practice, or am thinking of instructing one` THEN `yes if` (`Does a costs determination govern my fees` `the position`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Has the law practice breached its duty to tell me whether a costs determination applies, when it gave me its costs disclosure (Application Act s 143)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the law practice gave me the s 174(1)(a) costs disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice gave you the costs disclosure under Uniform Law s 174(1)(a)
      `it told me whether a costs determination applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it also told you whether a costs determination applies
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Has the law practice breached its duty to tell me whether a costs determination applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a client of a law practice, or am thinking of instructing one` THEN `yes if` (`Has my firm breached section 143` `the law practice gave me the s 174(1)(a) costs disclosure` `it told me whether a costs determination applies`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Application Act ss 149, 151 -- after a costs assessment`

@export As the client, can I still apply to the Supreme Court for review of the costs assessment (Application Act s 149(2)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the costs have been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the legal costs in the matter have been assessed under the Uniform Law and you have been notified of the assessment
      `the date I was notified` IS A DATE @desc The date you were notified of the costs assessment
      `the date I apply for review` IS A DATE @desc The date of the application for review
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`As the client can I still apply for review of the costs assessment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a client of a law practice, or am thinking of instructing one` THEN
        IF NOT (`the costs have been assessed`)
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can I still apply for review of the assessment` `the date I was notified` `the date I apply for review`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much must the law practice repay me as excess over the assessed costs (Application Act s 151)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the costs have been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the legal costs in the matter have been assessed under the Uniform Law and you have been notified of the assessment
      `what the client paid` IS A NUMBER @desc What the client paid as legal costs, in dollars
      `the assessed costs` IS A NUMBER @desc The legal costs determined on assessment, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much must the law practice repay me as excess over the assessed costs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a client of a law practice, or am thinking of instructing one` THEN
        IF NOT (`the costs have been assessed`)
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`How much must my firm repay` `what the client paid` `the assessed costs`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Uniform Law ss 6, 10 -- legal work by someone not entitled to do it`

@export Can the person who did legal work for me recover fees for it, if they were not entitled to engage in legal practice (Uniform Law ss 6, 10(2), 43; General Rules r 10)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what they did for me` IS A `What I want to do` @desc What the person did for you: legal advice or other legal services, or policy work only
      `their standing` IS A `My standing` @desc Whether the person is an Australian lawyer
      `they held a current practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person held a current Australian practising certificate when doing the work
      `they were authorised by another law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a law of the Commonwealth or a State, other than the Uniform Law, authorised the person to engage in legal practice
      `they were exempt under General Rules r 10` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a General Rules r 10 exemption covers what the person did (for example a licensed conveyancer)
GIVETH A `Recovery by an unqualified person`
`Can the person who did legal work for me recover fees if they were not entitled` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a client of a law practice, or am thinking of instructing one` THEN `for the client, what s 10(2) says of` (`May I engage in legal practice` `what they did for me` `their standing` `they held a current practising certificate` `they were authorised by another law` `they were exempt under General Rules r 10`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
